## Integrate an AI agent with Foundry IQ

# Create a Foundry project
# Create an agent
# Home > Build > Agent > Create
# Choose a name and model (gpt 4.1)

# give your agent the following instructions:
 You are a helpful AI assistant for Contoso, specializing in outdoor camping and hiking products. 
 You must ALWAYS search the knowledge base to answer questions about our products or product 
 catalog. Provide detailed, accurate information and always cite your sources.
 If you don't find relevant information in the knowledge base, say so clearly.
# Save

# Knowledge > Add , and select Connect to Foundry IQ > Create new resource

# Download this and extract 3 pdfs: https://github.com/MicrosoftLearning/mslearn-ai-agents/raw/main/Labfiles/04-integrate-agent-with-foundry-iq/data/contoso-products.zip

# Go to Azure portal, create in storage account and save in blob container
# Choose Azure Blob Storage as your knowledge source, then select Connect on your AI foundry

# Configure the Knowledge base settings
Name
Description
Storage account name
Container name
Authentication type: API Key
Content extraction mode: minimal
Embedding model: Select the available deployed model, likely text-embedding-3-small
Chat completions model: gpt 4.1
# Create

# On the knowledge base creation page, select the gpt-4.1 model from the Chat completions model dropdown, leaving the rest of the field defaults as is.

# Select Save knowledge base, and then refresh your browser to verify the knowledge source status is active.

# Select the back button to return to the Knowledge page, then select the Manage link next to the Connection drop-down.

# Scroll down to the Connected resources, where you should see your cognitivesearch service. Select that row, find the Authentication section, and select Edit authentication.

# Return to the Azure portal tab, Copy one of those keys from access keys into the dialog in Foundry and select Save. (Change to API authentication if otherwise)

## Test the Agent in the playground
# Navigate back to your agent on the Build > Agents page, and select the agent you created.

# Find the knowledge section and add Foundry IQ, selecting the connection and knowledge base you created.

# test queries to verify the agent can retrieve information from the knowledge base:
What types of tents does Contoso offer?
Tell me about which backpacks are available in XL.
What camping accessories are available?

# Review the responses and notice:
# The agent provides specific information from the knowledge base
# Citations or references to the source documents may be included
# The agent stays focused on product information

# Agent name: product-expert-agent
# Project endpoint: Found in the project settings or home page
https://agent-iq-prom-resource.services.ai.azure.com/api/projects/agent-iq-prom

